<title>UK: Littlewoods axes jobs as new lottery bites.</title>
<headline>Littlewoods axes jobs as new lottery bites.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retail to football pools company Littlewoods Group said on Tuesday it was cutting 426 jobs at Littlewoods Pools because the newly-launched midweek National Lottery was hitting revenues.</p>
<p>Littlewoods said its pools business employed 4,000 people before the National Lottery was started and, with the new job cuts, will now employ just over 1,000. Littlewoods Group employs over 30,000 people nationwide.</p>
<p>Last week, Littlewoods rival Vernons Pools, owned by betting and hotels chain Ladbroke Group Plc, also announced job cuts, saying the soccer pools market had halved since the National Lottery began.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
